  "draft_markdown": "## MA-S3: Dedicated Attention Reranking Loop (mech_sym:9773c5add7af1f92)\n\nThe mechanism `mech_sym:9773c5add7af1f92` implements a reranking loop that processes passage texts based on similarity scores. The process begins with temperature scaling of similarities, followed by sorting to determine relevance indices, and concludes with a nested loop that constructs the final reranked passages.\n\n### 1. Temperature Scaling and Sorting\n\nThe initial step involves scaling the similarity scores by a temperature parameter. This is formalized by the operation `similarities = similarities / self.cfg.temperature`. This scaling adjusts the distribution of similarity scores before they are used for ranking.\n\nFollowing the scaling, the system sorts the scores to identify the most relevant passages. This is captured by the operation `relevance_scores, indices = torch.sort(`. The sorting process produces both the sorted scores and the corresponding indices that map back to the original passages.\n\nThe sorting operation specifically targets the similarities tensor along a specific dimension. The configuration `similarities, dim=1, descending=True` indicates that the sorting is performed on the second dimension (dim=1) in descending order, ensuring the highest similarity scores are ranked first.\n\n### 2. Reranking Loop Initialization\n\nBefore the main loop begins, an empty list is initialized to store the final results. This is defined by `reranked_passages = []`. This list will eventually contain the reordered passage texts for each input item.\n\nThe main loop iterates over the batch dimension of the similarities tensor. The loop structure is defined by `for i in range(similarities.shape[0]):`. This ensures that each item in the batch is processed individually.\n\nWithin this outer loop, a temporary list is created for each batch item. This is initialized with `temp_reranked_passages = []`. This temporary list will hold the reordered passages for the current batch item before being appended to the final result.\n\n### 3. Inner Loop and Passage Retrieval\n\nThe inner loop iterates over the indices for the current batch item. This is defined by `for j in range(indices[i].shape[0]):`. This loop processes each ranked passage index for the current item.\n\nThe core of the reranking logic is the retrieval of the actual passage text based on the sorted indices. This is performed by `temp_reranked_passages.append(passage_text[i][indices[i][j]])`. This operation uses the index `j` to access the sorted indices for item `i`, which in turn retrieves the corresponding passage text from the `passage_text` structure.\n\nThe entire nested loop structure is encapsulated in the following block:\n\n```python\nfor i in range(similarities.shape[0]):\n    temp_reranked_passages = []\n    for j in range(indices[i].shape[0]):\n        temp_reranked_passages.append(passage_text[i][indices[i][j]])\n    reranked_passages.append(temp_reranked_passages)\n```\n\nThis loop structure ensures that the passages are reordered according to their relevance scores, with the highest-scoring passages appearing first in the `reranked_passages` list.",
